✅ Base Styling
Sets the global font to Roboto for modern readability.

Applies default background color (#f8f9fa) and text color (#333) for good contrast and readability.

Resets margin and padding for consistency across browsers.

🧭 Navbar Styling
The .navbar gets a dark background (#34495e) and padding for spacing.

.nav-list uses flexbox to align items horizontally with spacing between (gap: 2rem).

.nav-link styles links to:

Remove underlines.

Apply white bold text.

Change to yellow (#f1c40f) on hover for interactivity.

📄 Section Styling
.section gives each section consistent padding and a bottom border for visual separation.

🔻 Footer Styling
.footer uses the same background as the navbar for consistency.

Centers text and uses white color to contrast the dark background.

🔹 HTML Structure Overview
Your portfolio is structured using semantic HTML tags, ensuring both readability and accessibility.

✅ 1. <!DOCTYPE html> & <html lang="en">
Defines the document type and language, setting the foundation for the webpage.

✅ 2. <head> Section
Sets up meta tags for character encoding and responsive design.

Includes the Roboto font via Google Fonts.

Links to an external CSS file (styles.css) for styling.

🔹 Navigation (<header> + <nav>)
Contains a navbar with internal links: Home, About, Work, Resume, Contact.

Styled using CSS classes: .navbar, .nav-list, .nav-link.

🔹 Main Sections (<section>)
Each section is clearly marked for easy navigation:

#home: Welcomes users with a short intro.

Other sections like #about, #work, #resume, and #contact should be added and given the class section to ensure styling is consistent.

🔹 Footer
Contains a copyright.

Uses the class .footer for dark styling and centered white text.

🔹 Styling (from styles.css)
Sets a clean font and background color.

Navigation is styled as a horizontal menu with hover effects.

Sections have spacing and borders.

The footer has a dark background with white text.